We are not surprised when a two-year-old looks at a dog and says “doggie!
” because we are used to the miracle of children learning to recognize and name things.
Simon’s point is that the miracles of expert intuition have the same character.
Valid intuitions develop when experts have learned to recognize familiar elements in a new situation and to act in a manner that is appropriate to it.
Good intuitive judgments come to mind with the same immediacy as “doggie!
”
